WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:02.668
-Puerto Rico is in the midst

00:00:02.668 --> 00:00:04.604
of an<i> epic</i> humanitarian crisis

00:00:04.604 --> 00:00:06.606
after being struck
by Hurricane Maria.

00:00:06.606 --> 00:00:08.608
Most of the island is
without electricity

00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:11.411
or clean drinking water, people
are desperate and terrified,

00:00:11.411 --> 00:00:13.112
and the situation is only
gonna get worse

00:00:13.112 --> 00:00:14.681
in the coming days and weeks.

00:00:14.681 --> 00:00:17.249
So, naturally, President Trump
tweeted last night

00:00:17.249 --> 00:00:21.254 line:0%
that Puerto Rico has an...

00:00:21.254 --> 00:00:25.325 line:0%
and that they owe money to...

00:00:25.325 --> 00:00:28.294
Which brings us to a segment
we call "Hey!"

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:30.863
[ Suspenseful music climbs ]

00:00:30.863 --> 00:00:32.264
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:32.264 --> 00:00:33.532
Hey!

00:00:33.532 --> 00:00:34.934
Don't go after Puerto Rico

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:37.503
for their financial
problems<i> now.</i>

00:00:37.503 --> 00:00:40.539
Victims of tragedy aren't
lookin' for real talk.

00:00:40.539 --> 00:00:42.608
You don't start a eulogy
by saying, "Well,

00:00:42.608 --> 00:00:44.277
the guy never exercised."

00:00:44.277 --> 00:00:46.179
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.179 --> 00:00:47.814
And, hey, weren't you the guy

00:00:47.814 --> 00:00:50.149
who was gonna put Americans
before Wall Street?

00:00:50.149 --> 00:00:52.151
You couldn't even do that
in a tweet!

00:00:52.151 --> 00:00:54.020
People don't have
clean drinking water

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:56.622
and your first instinct is
to tell them they owe money.

00:00:56.622 --> 00:00:58.524
What are you, some kind
of [bleep] landlord?

00:00:58.524 --> 00:01:00.960
[ Laughter ]
Oh, right,

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.795
you were a [bleep] landlord.

00:01:02.795 --> 00:01:04.797
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:04.797 --> 00:01:07.800
[ Whistling ]
Hey,

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:10.970
thank God -- thank God
you didn't go to Vietnam.

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:12.872
I can see it now:
Trump, I'm hit!

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:14.040
Get the medic!

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:15.542
[as Trump]
You still owe me $20.

00:01:15.542 --> 00:01:16.909
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.909 --> 00:01:18.878
And, hey, it took you
a full week

00:01:18.878 --> 00:01:21.981
before you even sent someone
to check out the situation.

00:01:21.981 --> 00:01:24.016
For a guy with such
a crooked little boner

00:01:24.016 --> 00:01:27.053
for first responders,
you sure are the last responder.

00:01:27.053 --> 00:01:28.788
-[Laughter] Ohh!
-You're like the guy

00:01:28.788 --> 00:01:30.556
who says he'll help
his friend move

00:01:30.556 --> 00:01:32.826
and then just shows up
at the end for pizza.

00:01:32.826 --> 00:01:34.727
[ Laughter ]
And, hey, Puerto Ricans

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:36.162
<i> are</i> Americans.

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:39.365
They use American currency
and carry American passports.

00:01:39.365 --> 00:01:41.434
There's an Applebee's
in San Juan

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:43.469
and Americans in San Juan
go there

00:01:43.469 --> 00:01:45.672
to get disappointed
by American food.

00:01:45.672 --> 00:01:46.806
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.806 --> 00:01:48.240
You wanted to make America
great again,

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:51.143
so I'll say it again:
Puerto Rico is America.

00:01:51.143 --> 00:01:52.645
They're included in the whole

00:01:52.645 --> 00:01:54.613
"Make America great again"
thing.

00:01:54.613 --> 00:01:56.882
Though, let's be honest,
some Puerto Ricans are already

00:01:56.882 --> 00:01:58.250
as great as it gets.

00:01:58.250 --> 00:01:59.552
[ Laughter and cheering ]

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:01.053
[ Applause ]
This has been "Hey!"

00:02:01.053 --> 00:02:04.057
[ Suspenseful music climbs ]
[ Cheering and applause ]

